{"title":"initiation of the artist warrior monk, libra I","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/libra-i-the-artist","date":1759570140000,"content":"<figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/94d65a14-03cb-4a2d-a616-a7eccc5c6ea0/libra+I+the+artist.png?format=1000w\" width=\"3840\" height=\"2160\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/94d65a14-03cb-4a2d-a616-a7eccc5c6ea0/libra+I+the+artist.png?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/94d65a14-03cb-4a2d-a616-a7eccc5c6ea0/libra+I+the+artist.png?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/94d65a14-03cb-4a2d-a616-a7eccc5c6ea0/libra+I+the+artist.png?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/94d65a14-03cb-4a2d-a616-a7eccc5c6ea0/libra+I+the+artist.png?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/94d65a14-03cb-4a2d-a616-a7eccc5c6ea0/libra+I+the+artist.png?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/94d65a14-03cb-4a2d-a616-a7eccc5c6ea0/libra+I+the+artist.png?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/94d65a14-03cb-4a2d-a616-a7eccc5c6ea0/libra+I+the+artist.png?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p><em>an illustration inspired by my collaboration with LJ of </em><a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Ceremony</em></a><em> for their communal writing practice, </em><a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/atmospheres\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Atmospheres</em></a><em>, guided by the 36 decans of the astrological year. </em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p><strong><em>Libra I</em></strong><em> — </em>23 September – 3 October<em><br /></em><strong><em>Key themes from LJ</em></strong><em> — </em>Initiation, Artistry, Commitment<em><br /></em><strong><em>before this: </em></strong><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/virgo-iii-bruise-violet\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Bruise Violet, Virgo III</em></a><em><br /><br />*</em></p><p>this illustration for Libra (I) was, in part, very much inspired by the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_of_Swords\" target=\"_blank\">two of swords</a>. I used to find this card puzzlingly frustrating — a card of defense and stuckness — until I’ve realized, through working with LJ, to see it as a card of meditation and initiation into the sacred discipline of <em>being an artist.</em> </p><p>there is something about wielding two swords — cold sharpness against the illusive softness of the lunar, watery landscape — that feels like the tension between that of control and surrender, willpower and fate, the sharp faculties of the thinking mind — versus the fluid territories of the creative psyche. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e140f50d-d591-48a9-b6ab-38e77d56193c/two+of+swords.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"1121\" height=\"1920\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e140f50d-d591-48a9-b6ab-38e77d56193c/two+of+swords.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e140f50d-d591-48a9-b6ab-38e77d56193c/two+of+swords.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e140f50d-d591-48a9-b6ab-38e77d56193c/two+of+swords.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e140f50d-d591-48a9-b6ab-38e77d56193c/two+of+swords.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e140f50d-d591-48a9-b6ab-38e77d56193c/two+of+swords.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e140f50d-d591-48a9-b6ab-38e77d56193c/two+of+swords.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e140f50d-d591-48a9-b6ab-38e77d56193c/two+of+swords.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p>being an artist feels like this — like something between being a warrior and a monk; poised in stillness and meditation, yet ready for movement at any moment. </p><p>it is recognizing that you hold immense power in your hands — <em>the sword represents your creative power, or it represents your capacity for truth, clarity, vision, creation/destruction at the same time</em>. and yet, you are willingly blind-folded. here, this blind-folding doesn’t signal deliberate blindness or weakness, but conviction in your own ability.</p><p>there is such a history of blind prophets and warriors — as if the act of closing the outer vision creates heightened inner vision and perceptiveness. </p><p>what do we see with our eyes closed, with our backs turned from the watery moon, while wielding the sharpness of our creative power in our hands? </p><p>do we remember their presence? </p><p>perhaps, part of the initiation of the artist, then, is two-fold:</p><ol><li><p><strong><em>embracing the blindfold</em></strong> — turning inwards to inner vision, no matter where you are, being able to practice closing your eyes to what is obvious, and sensing what’s beneath </p></li><li><p><strong><em>awareness of swords</em></strong> — cultivating a deeper relationship to the presence of your creative power — to see it as training, not unlike martial arts or monkhood. for me, this sword represents truth, beauty, wisdom, knowing. </p></li></ol>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <h1>process</h1>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/007f8a08-0b62-425e-808f-7ed4950817f3/libraI-theartist-process-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=1000w\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/007f8a08-0b62-425e-808f-7ed4950817f3/libraI-theartist-process-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/007f8a08-0b62-425e-808f-7ed4950817f3/libraI-theartist-process-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/007f8a08-0b62-425e-808f-7ed4950817f3/libraI-theartist-process-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/007f8a08-0b62-425e-808f-7ed4950817f3/libraI-theartist-process-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/007f8a08-0b62-425e-808f-7ed4950817f3/libraI-theartist-process-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/007f8a08-0b62-425e-808f-7ed4950817f3/libraI-theartist-process-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/007f8a08-0b62-425e-808f-7ed4950817f3/libraI-theartist-process-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p><strong>explore</strong> <a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/atmospheres\" target=\"_blank\">atmospheres</a><br /><strong>see all</strong> <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal\" target=\"_blank\">atmospheres illustrations</a><br /><strong>more</strong> <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/visual-art\" target=\"_blank\">visual art</a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"ce97d32511e40f47d9e857f8993e2abca249a37633295b2f4e8d603d015f4fdc","category":"Sites"}